## RIG-64 — Radar Mounting Requirements for Unitree B2

**1. Mounting Height**

The Texas Instruments AWR1443 radar will be installed above the Unitree B2's LiDAR sensor, 
during CAD development, an approximate 10 mm above the LiDAR was used as a reference for positioning the mounting system.



**2. Field of View (FoV)**

The radar will face backward with a 15° inclination relative to the horizontal reference plane, 
this orientation was defined to direct the radar's detection area toward the region in front of the robot.

The enclosure uses an open-frame design to minimize obstruction of the radar.

**3. Cable Routing**

The radar cable will exit through the enclosure's open structure and be routed toward the Unitree B2's onboard processing module or computer, 
the enclosure provides access to the radar connectors without requiring complete disassembly of the case.

**4. Printing Material**

The enclosure and mounting components will be manufactured using PLA (Polylactic Acid) through FDM 3D printing, 
PLA was selected for its ease of printing, dimensional accuracy, and rigidity.

**5. Mechanical Mounting**

A custom modular mounting system was designed in Autodesk Inventor 2027 to integrate the radar enclosure with the Unitree B2, 
the system consists of a rectangular enclosure with long and short side frames, corner connectors, and mounting components.
